# Named `Dockerfile.dockerignore`, not `.dockerignore`, and lives here in deploy/ rather than the
# repo root — Docker's own convention: for a build invoked with `-f deploy/Dockerfile` (see
# deploy/docker-compose*.yml, context is the repo root), it looks for `<that same path>
# .dockerignore` in the context root before falling back to a plain `.dockerignore` there. Since
# `deploy/Dockerfile.dockerignore` is itself a valid path within the repo-root context, this
# resolves to this exact file (verified empirically) — a Dockerfile-specific ignore file physically
# alongside the Dockerfile it governs, instead of at the repo root.
.git
# Dockerignore matching is NOT gitignore-style — a bare pattern like `.venv` only matches at the
# context root, not at any depth (unlike git's own .gitignore). `**/` is required to match these
# wherever they actually occur (api/.venv, api/**/__pycache__, etc).
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
webui/node_modules
api/static/workspace
api/tests
